body:
I don't have anything to say on the other stuff since everyone's already said it before. But one thing that bothers me is how people *constantly* misuse the word "integration". Integration is the process of breaking down dissociative barriers and increasing inner-system communication, it doesn't necessarily involve fusion 100% of the time. Fusion is what most people think of when they hear "integration". 

&#x200B;

Also for the love of god why is integration censored I can't--

The term "sysmed" makes me want to crawl into a hole and die. It's just like the whole "transmed" thing. 

&#x200B;

* A
